import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'door-close':('A floor grid turns into a closed door','The Borg has a flow routed through a floor grid (flow value 50, knowledge recorded, stone-to-mud stamps set). Between two map passes the door on that grid closes. The original takes the grid\'s old wall state after overwriting it with the new feature, sees no change and keeps everything stale; the correction invalidates the flow (value 255), clears knowledge and resets the wizard-light and detect-walls stamps.'),
 'door-open':('A closed door opens','The same grid changes from a closed door to floor. The flow value stays (only new walls get 255) but knowledge and the stamps are cleared in the corrected version; the original keeps everything stale.'),
 'no-change':('Control: the grid is unchanged','With no feature change between the passes nothing is invalidated in either version. The complete logs are byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/mapwall-212 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('SETUP pass1','setup'),('STATE ','state'),('OUTCOME ','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>New walls and doors never left the Borg's flow</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native map passes</p><h1>New walls and doors never left the Borg's flow</h1><p>When a grid changes between map passes — a door closes, a tunnel is dug, a wall appears — the Borg is supposed to drop that grid from its routing flows, refresh what it knows, recalculate its view and light, and reset the wizard-light and detect-walls stamps. But the map pass read the grid's "old" wall state after it had already overwritten the grid with the new feature, so old and new always matched and the whole change block was dead: stale flows through freshly closed doors survived, and the Borg kept routing through walls. The correction reads the old state before the overwrite.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The grid</button><button data-step="1">After the second pass</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>With no feature change between the passes, nothing is invalidated in either version and the logs match byte for byte — the correction changes only the changed-grid cases.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior, depth 30, glowing constructed arena, one watched grid two grids east of the Borg. Between the two production map passes the fixture sets the game feature (a door closes, or opens). Flow, knowledge, icky flags and the stamps are planted before the second pass in the state a flow routine and a stone-to-mud detection would have left — recorded as a fixture intervention. The tracked state after the pass is read back; no movement or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/212">issue212</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}
function stateLabel(c){if(!c||!c.state)return'?';const parts=[];parts.push(`flow ${c.state.flow}`);parts.push(c.state.know?'know kept':'know cleared');parts.push(c.state.wizard_light?'stamps kept':'stamps reset');return parts.join(', ')}
function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`Grid starts ${c.label.includes('closed door')?'a closed door':'floor'}.`:stateLabel(d);p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'The Borg holds a flow and detection stamps on this grid.':'The second map pass sees the change.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===1?(d.state&&d.state.flow255?'Flow invalidated (255).':'Stale state kept.'):'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}
document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='no-change'?'Both versions agree in this control; the logs match byte for byte.':'The original keeps the stale state; the correction invalidates it.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}
select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
